Homework #7 - Week 12

In this practice I used K-means to group the data and find patterns. First I used price and total revenue using a scaler because kmeans works with distances and big numbers can change the result. I checked the elbow graph to find K and the line stops going down fast at 3 so I used 3 clusters. I saw three groups low price and revenue, medium, and high, the silhouette score was 0.4664 is not perfect but it is an acceptable. For the second test I used rating and quantity sold, I selected these columns because I know from past weeks that they don't have a relation so I wanted to see the result in kmeans. I did the same process and the score was 0.421, but the plot didnt make real groups, the points look like straight lines and not clusters. Conclusion I saw that kmeans is better when the data has a real relation like price and revenue and if the columns are not related the algorithm doesnt have a real meaning